{
  "id": "minimum-path-sum",
  "questionId": "minimum-path-sum",
  "slug": "minimum-path-sum",
  "title": "Minimum Path Sum",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Dp 2d",
  "patterns": [
    "dynamic programming",
    "grid"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "to reach cell (i, j) cheaply, you must have arrived from either directly above or directly to the left - which one is better depends only on the cheaper of those two paths",
    "define dp[i][j] as the minimum path sum to reach cell (i, j) from the start",
    "recurrence: dp[i][j] = grid[i][j] + min(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1])",
    "the first row can only be reached by moving right the whole way, and the first column only by moving down the whole way - fill those as running sums first",
    "fill the rest of the table row by row (or column by column) and return dp[m-1][n-1]"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "forgetting to initialize the first row and first column as running sums instead of trying to apply the general min() recurrence to them",
    "taking the max instead of the min by mistake when combining the two incoming paths",
    "not adding grid[i][j] itself into dp[i][j], only propagating the neighbor minimum"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a grid of non-negative integers. Starting at the top-left corner and moving only right or down at each step, you travel to the bottom-right corner.\n\n**Return the minimum possible sum of all numbers along such a path.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= rows <= 200",
      "1 <= cols <= 200",
      "0 <= grid[i][j] <= 100"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "a grid with a single cell",
      "a single row or single column grid (only one possible path)",
      "a grid where all cells have the same value"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "grid = [[1,3,1],[1,5,1],[4,2,1]]",
        "output": "7",
        "expectedOutput": "7",
        "explanation": "The path 1 -> 3 -> 1 -> 1 -> 1 sums to 7 and is the cheapest route."
      },
      {
